 <div class="mobile-on-page"><details><summary>On this page</summary><a href="#overview">Overview</a><a href="#dates">2027-29 Dates</a><a href="#admission">Admission</a><a href="#cutoff">CAT Cutoff</a><a href="#fees">Fees</a><a href="#programmes">Programmes</a><a href="#placements">Placements</a><a href="#fit">Who Should Apply?</a><a href="#faq">FAQs</a></details></div><div class="page-layout"><aside class="sidebar"><div class="sidebar-card"><div class="sidebar-title">On this page</div><a href="#overview">College Overview</a><a href="#dates">2027-29 Dates</a><a href="#admission">Admission Process</a><a href="#cutoff">CAT Cutoff</a><a href="#fees">Fees</a><a href="#programmes">Popular Programmes</a><a href="#placements">Placements</a><a href="#fit">Who Should Apply?</a><a href="#faq">FAQs</a></div></aside><main class="content"><section class="main-section" id="overview"><h2>IIM Bangalore: Key Facts for Applicants</h2><p><strong>Indian Institute of Management Bangalore (IIMB)</strong> offers degree programmes for recent graduates, experienced professionals and research candidates. Its management options include the two-year full-time PGP MBA, two-year PGPBA in Business Analytics, one-year EPGP for experienced professionals, weekend PGPEM for working professionals and the hybrid PGPPM in public policy.</p><p>Applicants should compare each programme by work experience, study format and admission test rather than treating all IIMB programmes as the same MBA route. IIMB also offers a doctoral programme. See the <a href="https://www.iimb.ac.in/programmes" rel="noopener" target="_blank">official IIM Bangalore programme list</a> for the current portfolio.</p><div class="highlight-grid"><div class="highlight"><strong>540</strong><span>PGP students enrolled in 2026</span></div><div class="highlight"><strong>77</strong><span>PGPBA students enrolled in 2026</span></div><div class="highlight"><strong>2 years</strong><span>PGP residential format</span></div></div></section><hr/><section class="main-section" id="dates"><h2>What Are the Admission Timelines for IIM Bangalore Programmes?</h2><p><strong>PGP domestic dates for 2027–29 have not yet been confirmed on IIMB’s official admissions page.</strong> PGP dates below are planning estimates. The PGPBA dates are published by IIMB and remain subject to change.</p><div aria-label="Scrollable data table" class="table-wrapper" role="region" tabindex="0"><table><tr><th scope="col">Admission event</th><th scope="col">Timeline</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr><tr><td>PGP application</td><td><strong>Oct 2026–Jan 2027</strong></td><td>Tentative</td></tr><tr><td>CAT registration/exam</td><td>As per official CAT 2026 schedule</td><td>Check official CAT notice</td></tr><tr><td>PGP shortlist/interview</td><td><strong>Feb–Mar 2027</strong></td><td>Tentative</td></tr><tr><td>PGP final offers</td><td><strong>Apr 2027</strong></td><td>Tentative</td></tr><tr><td>PGPBA applications open</td><td><strong>1 October 2026</strong></td><td>Published*</td></tr><tr><td>PGPBA applications close</td><td><strong>14 January 2027</strong></td><td>Published*</td></tr><tr><td>PGPBA interviews</td><td><strong>February–March 2027</strong></td><td>Published*</td></tr><tr><td>PGPBA offers</td><td><strong>Second week of April 2027</strong></td><td>Published*</td></tr></table></div><p class="notice"><strong>Planning note:</strong> PGP dates are estimates until IIMB publishes the domestic schedule. <a href="https://www.iimb.ac.in/node/9792" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Check IIMB’s published PGPBA dates</a>. Published dates are subject to change.</p></section><hr/><section class="main-section" id="admission"><h2>How Does Admission Work Across IIM Bangalore Programmes?</h2><p>The steps below describe the domestic flagship PGP route. PGPBA, EPGP and PGPEM use programme-specific criteria; compare the <a href="/iim-bangalore-pgpba">IIM Bangalore MBA in Business Analytics (PGPBA)</a>, <a href="/iim-bangalore-epgp">IIM Bangalore Executive MBA (EPGP)</a> and <a href="/iim-bangalore-pgpem">IIM Bangalore Weekend MBA (PGPEM)</a> admissions pages before applying.</p><h3>Flagship PGP MBA: eligibility and selection</h3><h3>1. Check academic eligibility</h3><p>For the flagship PGP, applicants need a bachelor's degree in any discipline with at least <strong>50% marks or equivalent CGPA</strong>. The minimum is <strong>45%</strong> for SC, ST and PwD candidates, subject to the current admission document.</p><h3>2. Take CAT</h3><p>Domestic PGP admission uses the <strong>Common Admission Test (CAT)</strong>. CAT is one part of IIMB's selection process.</p><h3>3. Clear the first shortlist</h3><p>IIMB applies published section-wise and aggregate CAT requirements and considers other prescribed factors such as academics, work experience/professional qualification and diversity.</p><h3>4. Attend WAT and PI</h3><p>Shortlisted candidates proceed to the institute's <strong>Written Ability Test and Personal Interview</strong> stage as specified for the admission cycle.</p><h3>5. Receive the final offer</h3><p>The final composite score uses the components prescribed in the relevant admission policy. <strong>Meeting the minimum CAT percentile does not guarantee an interview call or admission.</strong></p></section><hr/><section class="main-section" id="cutoff"><h2>Which Admission Requirements Should IIM Bangalore Applicants Check?</h2><h3>Flagship PGP MBA: Latest published CAT screening thresholds</h3><p>For the flagship PGP 2026–28 batch, IIMB published the following minimum CAT percentile requirements for the first-shortlist process. These are <strong>the latest published historical thresholds, not the confirmed 2027–29 cutoff or a guarantee of admission</strong>. See the <a href="https://www.iimb.ac.in/sites/default/files/inline-files/PGP-2026%20admissions%20process.pdf" rel="noopener" target="_blank">official PGP admission process</a> and the <a href="/iim-bangalore-pgpba">separate PGPBA cutoff guide</a>.</p><div aria-label="Scrollable data table" class="table-wrapper" role="region" tabindex="0"><table><tr><th scope="col">Category</th><th scope="col">VARC</th><th scope="col">DILR</th><th scope="col">QA</th><th scope="col">Aggregate</th></tr><tr><td>General</td><td>80</td><td>75</td><td>75</td><td><strong>85</strong></td></tr><tr><td>NC-OBC</td><td>70</td><td>65</td><td>65</td><td><strong>75</strong></td></tr><tr><td>EWS</td><td>70</td><td>65</td><td>65</td><td><strong>75</strong></td></tr><tr><td>SC</td><td>65</td><td>60</td><td>60</td><td><strong>70</strong></td></tr><tr><td>ST</td><td>55</td><td>55</td><td>55</td><td><strong>65</strong></td></tr><tr><td>PwD</td><td>50</td><td>50</td><td>50</td><td><strong>60</strong></td></tr></table></div><div class="answer-box"><strong>How should you read this?</strong><p>IIMB's published minimum is a screening requirement. Actual interview calls and final admission depend on the complete selection methodology.</p></div></section><hr/><section class="main-section" id="fees"><h2>What Are the Published Fees for IIM Bangalore Programmes?</h2><h3>PGP MBA fee for the 2026–28 batch</h3><p>For the domestic PGP 2026-28 batch, IIMB publishes a two-year programme fee of <strong>₹26,00,000</strong>, plus a <strong>₹30,000 refundable caution deposit</strong>. A mess advance of <strong>₹30,000 per term</strong> is payable separately.</p><h3>Fee bifurcation</h3><div aria-label="Scrollable data table" class="table-wrapper" role="region" tabindex="0"><table><tr><th scope="col">Component</th><th scope="col">PGP 2026-28</th></tr><tr><td>Programme fee</td><td><strong>₹26,00,000</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Refundable caution deposit</td><td><strong>₹30,000</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Mess advance</td><td><strong>₹30,000 per term</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Taxes/other applicable charges</td><td>As applicable</td></tr></table></div><h3>What the fee covers</h3><ul><li>Tuition and academic-related charges</li><li>Library and internet</li><li>Case permission royalty and course material</li><li>Hostel room rent and service charge</li><li>Medical and personal accident insurance</li><li>Alumni activity</li></ul><h3>What the fee does not cover</h3><ul><li><strong>Mess advance</strong></li><li><strong>Refundable caution deposit</strong></li><li>Any charge stated by IIMB as payable separately or applicable taxes</li></ul><p><strong>Budgeting note:</strong> Do not infer a complete two-year living cost from the ₹26 lakh programme fee because mess and personal expenses vary.</p></section><hr/><section class="main-section" id="programmes"><h2>Which Programmes Can You Study at IIM Bangalore?</h2><p>The routes below differ in duration, format and intended experience level. Choose the dedicated programme page for detailed admission criteria, fees and selection rules.</p><div class="programme-grid"><div class="programme-card"><span class="programme-label">2 years · CAT</span><h3>PGP – MBA</h3><p>Full-time residential flagship MBA for candidates seeking broad management training.</p><a class="programme-link" href="/iim-bangalore-mba">IIM Bangalore MBA (PGP): eligibility, CAT selection and fees →</a></div><div class="programme-card"><span class="programme-label">2 years · CAT</span><h3>PGPBA – MBA Business Analytics</h3><p>Full-time residential MBA focused on analytics and AI.</p><a class="programme-link" href="/iim-bangalore-pgpba">IIM Bangalore MBA in Business Analytics (PGPBA): admissions and fees →</a></div><div class="programme-card"><span class="programme-label">1 year · GMAT/GRE</span><h3>EPGP – MBA</h3><p>One-year residential MBA for experienced professionals with at least five years of post-graduation work experience.</p><a class="programme-link" href="/iim-bangalore-epgp">IIM Bangalore Executive MBA (EPGP): eligibility and admissions →</a></div><div class="programme-card"><span class="programme-label">2 years · Weekend</span><h3>PGPEM – MBA</h3><p>Weekend MBA designed for working professionals with substantial post-graduation experience.</p><a class="programme-link" href="/iim-bangalore-pgpem">IIM Bangalore Weekend MBA (PGPEM): admissions and fees →</a></div><div class="programme-card"><span class="programme-label">14 months · Hybrid</span><h3>PGPPM – Public Policy</h3><p>Hybrid programme for working professionals, including applicants from government, infrastructure, CSR and related sectors; IIMB lists a minimum of five years of work experience.</p><a class="programme-link" href="https://www.iimb.ac.in/programmes/pgppm" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Official IIM Bangalore Public Policy programme details →</a></div><div class="programme-card"><span class="programme-label">5 years · Full-time</span><h3>Doctoral Programme (PhD)</h3><p>Research-focused programme for candidates pursuing academic and high-quality management research.</p><a class="programme-link" href="https://www.iimb.ac.in/programmes/doctoral-programme" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Official IIM Bangalore PhD programme details →</a></div><div class="programme-card"><span class="programme-label">Undergraduate</span><h3>BBA in Digital Business and Entrepreneurship</h3><p>Online undergraduate degree programme; check the official programme site for current eligibility and admissions.</p><a class="programme-link" href="https://dbe.iimb.ac.in/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Official BBA DBE programme details →</a></div><div class="programme-card"><span class="programme-label">Undergraduate · 4 years</span><h3>BSc (Honours) programmes</h3><p>IIMB lists undergraduate programmes in Data Sciences and Economics. Mathematics and entrance requirements apply; verify the current admissions notice.</p><a class="programme-link" href="https://www.iimb.ac.in/programmes" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Official IIM Bangalore programme list →</a></div></div></section><hr/><section class="main-section" id="placements"><h2>What Do IIM Bangalore Placement Reports Show?</h2><p>The official 2026 placement report covers the <strong>PGP and PGPBA 2024–26 batch</strong>, reporting 605 students, 665 offers and 177 companies. A separate IIMB announcement reports 596 students appearing and 664 offers from 177 firms; the official communications use different counts, so these figures should not be merged. These numbers do not represent EPGP or PGPEM outcomes.</p><div class="highlight-grid"><div class="highlight"><strong>₹35.35 LPA</strong><span>Average salary · 2026 report</span></div><div class="highlight"><strong>₹34.75 LPA</strong><span>Median salary · 2026 report</span></div><div class="highlight"><strong>Not reported</strong><span>Highest CTC in reviewed official 2026 report</span></div></div><h3>Three-year comparable placement view</h3><div aria-label="Scrollable data table" class="table-wrapper" role="region" tabindex="0"><table><tr><th scope="col">Graduating year</th><th scope="col">Students placed</th><th scope="col">Median salary</th></tr><tr><td>2024-25</td><td>588</td><td><strong>₹32.61 lakh</strong></td></tr><tr><td>2023-24</td><td>517</td><td><strong>₹32.50 lakh</strong></td></tr><tr><td>2022-23</td><td>502</td><td><strong>₹33.00 lakh</strong></td></tr></table></div><p><strong>Placement rate:</strong> A percentage placement rate is not stated in the reviewed official 2026 placement report, so no rate is inferred. Management Consulting accounted for <strong>45% of offers</strong> in the 2026 cycle.</p><p class="notice"><strong>Important:</strong> Do not mix these final-placement figures with summer internship outcomes or with EPGP/PGPEM outcomes.</p><p>These figures apply to the reported PGP and PGPBA cohort, not every programme at IIMB. For programme-wise context and year-specific figures, see <a class="programme-link" href="/iim-bangalore-placements">IIM Bangalore placements: salary, offers and recruiters</a>.</p></section><hr/><section class="main-section" id="fit"><h2>Which IIM Bangalore Programme Fits Your Profile?</h2><div class="two-column"><div class="pro-box"><h3>PGP may suit applicants who</h3><ul><li>Want a two-year full-time residential MBA.</li><li>Are applying through CAT.</li><li>Want broad management exposure before selecting career domains.</li><li>Can commit to a full-time residential programme.</li></ul></div><div class="warning-box"><h3>Check before applying</h3><ul><li>Do not use the minimum CAT cutoff as a guaranteed-call percentile.</li><li>Compare fees only after checking what each programme includes.</li><li>EPGP and PGPEM have different work-experience expectations and formats.</li></ul></div></div></section><hr/><section class="main-section" id="faq"><h2>IIM Bangalore FAQs</h2><details class="accordion"><summary>What is the IIM Bangalore MBA entrance exam?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The flagship PGP and PGPBA use <strong>CAT</strong> for domestic admission. EPGP and PGPEM have separate published selection routes. Check the IIM Bangalore MBA (PGP) admission page, IIM Bangalore MBA in Business Analytics (PGPBA), IIM Bangalore Executive MBA (EPGP) and IIM Bangalore Weekend MBA (PGPEM) pages for programme-specific requirements.</p></div></details><details class="accordion"><summary>What is the IIM Bangalore MBA fee?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The published PGP 2026–28 programme fee is <strong>₹26 lakh</strong> for two years, plus a ₹30,000 refundable caution deposit and mess advance of ₹30,000 per term. This is the PGP fee, not a common fee for every IIMB programme. For other formats, check the official programme fee notice and the dedicated IIM Bangalore Executive MBA (EPGP) and IIM Bangalore Weekend MBA (PGPEM) pages before budgeting.</p></div></details><details class="accordion"><summary>What is the latest IIM Bangalore MBA average salary?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The official 2026 placement report records an <strong>₹35.35 lakh average salary</strong> and <strong>₹34.75 lakh median salary</strong> for the PGP and PGPBA 2024-26 batch.</p></div></details><details class="accordion"><summary>What is the IIM Bangalore CAT cutoff?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>For 2026-28, the published minimum aggregate percentile was <strong>85 for General</strong>, 75 for NC-OBC/EWS, 70 for SC, 65 for ST and 60 for PwD. These are minimum requirements, not guaranteed admission cutoffs.</p></div></details><details class="accordion"><summary>Does IIM Bangalore have an MBA for experienced professionals?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. EPGP is a one-year full-time MBA for experienced professionals, while PGPEM is a two-year weekend MBA for working professionals. Their eligibility and entrance requirements differ from the flagship PGP.</p></div></details><details class="accordion"><summary>Does IIM Bangalore publish a highest package?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The reviewed official 2026 placement report does not publish a highest CTC figure. This page therefore does not estimate or import a third-party number.</p></div></details></section></main></div></div><script>const links=document.querySelectorAll('.sidebar a'),sections=document.querySelectorAll('.main-section');const observer=new IntersectionObserver(entries=>entries.forEach(e=>{if(e.isIntersecting){links.forEach(l=>l.classList.remove('active'));const a=document.querySelector('.sidebar a[href="#'+e.target.id+'"]');if(a)a.classList.add('active')}}),{rootMargin:'-15% 0px -70% 0px',threshold:0});sections.forEach(s=>observer.observe(s));document.querySelectorAll('.mobile-on-page a').forEach(a=>a.addEventListener('click',()=>document.querySelector('.mobile-on-page details')?.removeAttribute('open')));</script>
