 <div class="page-container"><div class="mobile-on-page"><details><summary>On this page</summary></details></div><div class="page-layout"><aside class="sidebar"><div class="sidebar-card"><div class="sidebar-title">On this page</div><a href="#eligibility">Eligibility</a><a href="#dates">2026 Dates</a><a href="#process">Application</a><a href="#weightage">Selection</a><a href="#documents">Documents</a><a href="#strategy">How to prepare</a><a href="#faq">FAQs</a></div></aside><main class="content"><section class="main-section" id="eligibility"><h2>MANAGE PGDM ABM Eligibility 2026</h2><p>The 2026-28 admission policy required a <strong>four-year bachelor's degree after Class 12</strong> in agriculture or an agriculture-related discipline from a recognised university/institute. The minimum marks were <strong>50%</strong>, relaxed to 45% for SC/ST/PwD candidates.</p><div class="table-wrapper"><table><thead><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>2026 policy</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Degree</td><td data-label="2026 policy">Bachelor's degree in Agriculture or specified allied disciplines</td></tr><tr><td>Education duration</td><td data-label="2026 policy">Minimum 4 years after XII/10+2</td></tr><tr><td>Marks</td><td data-label="2026 policy">50% general; 45% SC/ST/PwD</td></tr><tr><td>Entrance score</td><td data-label="2026 policy"><strong>Valid CAT 2025 score mandatory</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
